WEBVTT

00:37:58.579 --> 00:38:02.204
We've got a whole audience of listeners
who are trying to figure out how to get

00:38:02.204 --> 00:38:04.163
through the next year or
so of the pandemic.

00:38:04.621 --> 00:38:08.704
And given given all the difficult
conditions you've endured throughout your

00:38:08.788 --> 00:38:10.371
life and your career, I'm wondering,

00:38:10.371 --> 00:38:11.788
what advice do you have for

00:38:11.788 --> 00:38:16.496
for anybody who's just trying to figure
out how to stay, how to stay on track,

00:38:16.496 --> 00:38:20.413
how to avoid burning out, how to deal with
all the uncertainty we're facing?

00:38:20.788 --> 00:38:22.204
What what guidance do you have?

00:38:22.746 --> 00:38:27.079
Well, you know, there again, how can
you give a blanket guidance?

00:38:27.079 --> 00:38:29.038
Because the people are so different.

00:38:29.038 --> 00:38:31.329
I mean, some of them, the ones
who've lost their jobs,